WEBVTT

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.620
I unsheathe thee, Sword of Light!

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.000
Stop!

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.790
That's... That's...

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:03.830
The moment he said that,
the monster lifted its head and howled.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:06.910
It sounded like an ordinary howl,

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:11.000
no more threatening than
a dog howling in the distance.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:17.000
But as soon as its voice reverberated
across the area and filled the air...

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.790
I knit thee thus, Chainmail of Haloes!

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.290
Untangle these webs, Dancing Bronco!

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:34.910
Azalie!

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.750
It's me!

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.700
Please, don't run away!

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.290
Azalie!

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:53.620
"The Tower of Fangs"

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:01.160
It felt like a distant memory,
though not that many moons had passed.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.660
On the northwestern part of
the continent lies the Tower of Fangs,

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.790
a place that trained
the most powerful Sorcerers.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:14.290
And out of those sorcerers,
the best of the best were in Childman's class.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.540
Heartia.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:18.910
Hark, O Light!

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.120
Disappear.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.120
Leticia.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.410
Yes, sir.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.040
O Lightning!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.040
Slash.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.330
Aw, too bad.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.410
Where's Corgon?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:56.000
He was reading books
in the attic the last I saw him.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.290
He's actually in the tower?

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.620
That's rare.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.290
I don't know what we're going
to do about that vagabond.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:09.410
I really wish he'd tell me where
he runs off to since I'm the class monitor.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.580
Then you're next, Forte.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.370
I humbly decline training with you, Master.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:18.580
Jeez, you're not fun.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.250
Then I guess I'm next.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.540
Combination 2-7-5.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.910
O Ripple!

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.540
Well, that was fun, wasn't it?

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.040
I mean, I guess?

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.500
Right?!

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.370
This isn't a game.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.910
I know.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.500
Hark, O Light!

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:56.410
That's the Chaos Witch for you...

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.040
Untangle these webs,

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.950
Dancing Bronco!

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.120
What the?

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.540
It's those students from Childman's class again?

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.790
Azalie, you need to hold back more!

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:31.040
If I did, this wouldn't
be proper training, would it?

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.120
However, now you'll need
to write another apology.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.290
What?! No way! Again?

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:40.000
Ugh, this sucks! This is my 50th one!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.450
You were totally dropping hints...

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.250
How could you?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.540
I hope you don't get bored
and snap that in two, as well...

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.330
I'm not collecting instruments for fun!

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.160
I'm able to create magic with my voice,

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.830
so I figured I might be able
to do that with sound, too.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.370
So, you finished writing yet?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.910
Wait, why am I writing this apology anyw--

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.120
Because I'm sick of writing them.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:17.410
Then don't do anything that'd make
you write them in the first place!

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.620
Exactly.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:22.950
Cause any more issues and
Childman's class is going to disappear.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.790
The other classes hate us enough as is.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:29.870
They keep saying we're all gifted
but that we're also troublemakers.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:31.370
Is that why you're wearing that?

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.160
Yes. I applied to be a prefect.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.830
I need to keep all you rabble-rousers in check.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.120
Keep us in check?

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.870
Why do I feel like this is
all gonna fall back on me?

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.830
This time, I'm going to truly blow your minds!

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:51.540
At last! I was able to make this
mechanical battle soldier into compact size!

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.910
Necessity is truly the mother of all inventions!

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.950
And now, the name of this fabulous invention...

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:00.250
Why you!

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.080
Wh-What was that for?!

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:08.750
I call this, the Slayer of Failed Experiments,

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.160
the Goodbye Arch.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:13.950
How dare you! You shall face
the wrath of the Mighty Cog!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.580
You keep making these weird tin cans,

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.620
and we're always the ones
who have to clean up your mess!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.580
He's right. Do anything weird,
and I'll make you regret it!

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.450
Wait, what did I even do?!

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:30.000
I just sold one of your lipsticks
to one of your secret admirers.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.580
Wait, how could you?!

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:33.330
You're the worst!

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.200
O Lightning!

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.330
Talk about divine punishment.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.700
Yeah.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.040
Hey, wake up!

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:50.790
How long do you plan on sleeping?!

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:54.830
We got thrown in here because of you,
so wake your ass up!

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.080
Fraud, disturbing the peace,
damage to property...

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.830
How long is our sentence going to be

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.080
if they're trying to charge us with all this?!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.450
Hey, you stupid Sorcerer! Hurry up
and get us out of here with your magic!

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.450
If I actually wanted to leave,
I would've left a long time ago.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:14.040
I can open that lock in two seconds.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:17.160
But I'd rather not become
a wanted criminal just yet.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:20.410
Or rather, isn't fraud your specialty?

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:23.790
The real problem here is that monster!

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:29.700
Everyone there saw you talking
to that damn monster!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.160
Don't you dare call her a monster!

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.700
"H-Her"?!

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:43.290
Most kids tend to admire
any girl that's slightly older

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.450
than them and takes care of them.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.750
I mean, I knew you weren't exactly normal,

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.950
but I never would've guessed
that monster raised you.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.330
I see. That actually makes sense.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.620
I was raised at the Tower of Fangs.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:05.410
The Tower of Fangs? You mean
where the most powerful Sorcerers...

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:08.000
She's from there, too.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.290
Azalie, her cousin, and I

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.700
all entered the Tower of Fangs
from the same orphanage.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:19.330
We were orphans... Actually,
so were most of the Sorcerers there.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:25.700
If any of us actually had parents who
cared about us, they'd never send us there.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:29.660
Since only a few were able to survive
and actually graduate from that place.

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:34.750
So that mon-- I mean, she was human originally?

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:36.950
Yeah.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:53.330
So you've come all this way
to try to return her to normal?

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:54.790
I'd been searching for her,

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:57.950
but she finally appeared
when I was about to give up.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:02.330
But as long as I don't know
what kind of Sorcery she used,

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.160
there's really nothing I can do.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.750
Krylancelo.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:13.330
Actually, I guess you
call yourself "Orphen" now.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:14.450
Heartia!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.160
Let's go. Master's waiting for you.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.450
"The Totokanta branch of
The Continental Sorcerers' Association"

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.580
I had no idea you were in Totokanta.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.830
I'm the secretary here.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:41.700
Though I'm basically just a maid.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.200
I see that you haven't changed, Heartia.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.870
Yet you've changed quite a bit.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.450
It's been five years,

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:00.700
Krylancelo.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.200
Master's finally recovered.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:18.370
"5 years ago"

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.500
Whose funeral is this?

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.250
Azalie's.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.000
Are you trying to say she was in this coffin?

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.120
This obviously isn't her funeral!

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.830
Krylancelo...

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:02.330
You're scared that the reputation of
the Tower of Fangs is going to be tarnished,

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.500
so you're trying to get rid of her?

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.040
Do we need to spell it out for you?

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.910
She failed her experiment,
turned into a monster, and fled.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:14.410
That could become a stain
that'll ruin the Tower once and for all.

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:16.200
She's not a stain!

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:19.950
She's one of the best Sorcerers to
appear since this Tower was established!

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:23.540
Not only a master of Black Sorcery,
she mastered White Sorcery, too!

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:26.620
Yes. She was indeed an impressive Sorcerer.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:29.160
Not "was"! She's still alive!

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:32.330
Come on, stop! At this rate, you're--

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.790
Stop what?!

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:36.830
You're an elite at the Tower!

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.450
You just made it to the top of the class!

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.160
Shut up, Heartia!

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.500
The only reason I'm the top of the class
is because Azalie never took the exams.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.700
She always said they were pointless.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.870
You're trying to bury an empty coffin.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:53.700
So I'll go ahead and fill that coffin for you!

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:56.330
You can bury me!

00:12:56.330 --> 00:13:01.200
You can bury my name,
along with Azalie's memory.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:04.790
I'm going to find her.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.000
No matter how many years it may take!

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:11.120
Until then, my name is Orphen... an orphan!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:14.620
She's irreplaceable... and I'll be Orphen!

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.120
There was something I wanted
to ask you once you woke up.

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:24.830
She said that she was going to do
some kind of experiment with you.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:27.620
What was that experiment?

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:31.160
The activation of the Sword of Baldanders.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.160
The Sword of Baldanders?

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:39.450
But the experiment was a failure,
and the sword accidentally discharged,

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:41.870
leaving her in that state,

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:45.370
and myself in a coma.

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.450
I have finally awakened,
and now, she's also on the move again.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:53.160
I believe that she had also
been unconscious this whole time.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:58.080
But it's unknown if she still has
any awareness that she's Azalie.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:02.080
She may have retained some
of her memories and instincts.

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:06.790
The impulsive instinct to want
to return to her human form.

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:09.160
Why was that sword there?

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.250
That's what Master ordered

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.660
before he lost consciousness.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.160
That's what he ordered Forte to do.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.950
I've been close to the
Everlasting Family for quite some time.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.450
I wanted to make sure
no one else tried use that sword,

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:29.160
so I gave them the sword
to seal it in the mansion.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:32.540
So that's why she appeared there.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:36.950
Because she thought she may be able
to return to normal if she had the sword.

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:41.330
That's what I thought, as well, so I came here.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:44.250
We haven't been able to capture her though.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:48.750
I know you just recovered,
but you're definitely more powerful.

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:52.330
Even if Azalie is the most talented
prodigy to appear at that Tower.

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:55.160
With Black Sorcery, yes.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.580
But she has a trump card.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.700
White Sorcery.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:08.330
White Sorcerers have the ability
to control time and the mind.

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:11.290
It may not sound like much,
but it's extremely powerful.

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:16.660
So in order to fight a White Sorcerer,
you need as many Sorcerers as you can get.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:22.370
Especially skilled Black Sorcerers
who excel in fighting.

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:25.620
Are you trying to order me to kill her?

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:28.410
She's one of your students!

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:33.410
I'm not going to force you, but it'd be
a great help if you're willing to help us.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.450
I refuse!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:38.830
One of the former most powerful
Sorcerers has lost their mind

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.500
and has fled with a forbidden sword!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.910
If this gets out,
the Tower's authority will be lost!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:48.750
Not to mention, Krylancelo,
this is a chance to redeem yourself!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:49.660
If you help us out,

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:52.370
you'll be able to regain your
honor after abandoning the Tower!

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:55.330
Then you'll be able to return to the Tower...

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:56.410
I--

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:57.750
Both of you,

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.000
stop this pointless argument.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:06.410
Krylancelo, we are forming a squad
to go subjugate the monster tonight.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:09.450
How do you know where she'll be?

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:13.790
As soon as I arrived here,
I snuck into the Everlasting Family's mansion

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:18.200
and set a beacon into the Sword of Baldanders.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.450
So that I could continue to track her,
no matter how far she went.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:25.450
So you're always going
to be one step ahead of me.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:31.660
The only way you'll ever see her
again is if you help us subjugate her.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:34.250
Will you join us or not?

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.790
When are you leaving?

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:39.540
We will be leaving at sundown.
You should prepare until then.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:54.200
Orphen, your lunch is ready.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.370
Wait, are you trying to leave without paying?!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.580
That's not it.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:58.790
Then...

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.750
I've got some work to do.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:04.000
Oh, it must be hard being a moneylender.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.540
That's not it either!

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.250
But I can't guarantee that I'll be back.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:13.870
Time has begun to move again.
The time that had been stopped all this time.

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:16.700
You'll understand someday.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.620
Probably.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:25.330
My mother and sister are in bed,
Mister Marriage Fraud.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:27.290
I won't try that again!

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:29.830
Then are you here to fix stuff today?

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.290
Basically.

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.500
I repair thee,

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.290
Scars of the Sunset.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:47.700
Wow, what did all that mean?

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.500
It's not really that deep.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:54.250
It's important to use your voice as
a medium in order to create the Sorcery.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:57.750
I could just shout something
random, and it'd still activate.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:58.910
Really?

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.660
Pretty much.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:02.160
Repair.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.540
I didn't think you'd actually
come back to fix everything.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.790
Thanks!

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:15.040
I mean, if you were to actually pay me,
I'd be able to pay off my tab at the inn.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:19.580
Sadly, I don't have any money
I can personally give you.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.120
Will this work?

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.290
Come on, I was just kidding.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:29.120
A Sorcerer gave us this ring, too.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.700
Then Father gave it to me.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:40.830
Can you read these letters, Krylancelo?

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:42.870
Are these even letters?

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:45.500
They're ancient runes called Wyrd Glyphs.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:49.700
The letters on this ring say,
"Drop your weapon."

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:53.500
Basically, it guards the owner from disaster.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:56.330
Though I think it only works once.

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:57.580
Just once?

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:00.370
Yeah. The precision
of the letters isn't that great,

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.910
so I don't think this was made
by a very powerful Sorcerer.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:08.500
Sadly, it only fits on my pinky.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:12.950
I'm sure it was made for a girl who had
much daintier and prettier hands than me.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:16.370
I think that your hands are pretty, too, Azalie.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.290
Oh, how sweet.

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.080
Thanks, Krylancelo.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:25.450
Hey, maybe it was made for
a child rather than some dainty girl.

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:27.290
You might be right.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:32.120
That means we might be able
to use it without having to do a chant.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:33.580
Actually tonight, we're going

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:37.540
to be doing an experiment involving
ancient Sorcery just like this ring has.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:38.870
An experiment?

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:39.870
Yeah.

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:43.290
Master asked me
to decipher some Wyrd Glyphs,

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:46.410
though Master said the
experiment might be dangerous.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.200
But we're still going to do it.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:55.450
Is there something about that ring?

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:57.910
Did Forte bring this, as well?

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.080
Forte?

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:01.870
He's really tall and has long hair.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:04.000
Oh, yeah!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:08.620
He's the one who visited
my father from the Tower of Fangs!

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.700
So it was him...

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:13.080
Were you at the Tower of Fangs, too?

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:13.950
Yeah.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:17.450
This ring belonged to Azalie.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:18.790
Azalie...

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:27.330
Yesterday, you also called
that monster Azalie...

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.410
Does that mean that monster's Azalie?

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.250
She's not a monster.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.700
Azalie is...

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:43.660
I wanted to fix up your yard, too,
but I don't think I have time.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.330
Where are you going?

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:47.250
I'm going to go find her...

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.750
Are you going to capture her?

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:49.870
No...

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:54.450
I'm going to get to her before
they can kill her and run away with her.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:58.290
I'm going to protect her.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:14.660
It's time. Let's go.

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:20.370
So you did come.

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:24.870
Join the squad, but you're going
to have to lead the vanguard.

00:21:24.870 --> 00:21:28.290
We won't have to write
another apology even if you die.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:29.750
Let's go.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.250
So you did come, Krylancelo.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.870
Comicron...

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:54.120
Everyone here's experienced.
Of course, I'd know a few of them.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:57.330
I can't let my emotions get the best of me.

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:00.750
I'm going to protect her, no matter what.

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:39.750
Orphen, I'll look for her, too!

00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:42.080
It's too dangerous! I'm the only one
who's going to participate in this hunt.

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:43.910
I know how to handle a sword!

00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:46.910
And I'm a handful when I get angry.

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:46.910
"HEED MY CALL, BEAST"
